Aristotle, the philosopher, proposed the theory that every substance is composed of one or more of the four elements, which are earth, water, air, and fire.
To a large extent, it was similar to the four states of matter: solid, liquid, gas, and plasma; although he also proposed the idea that they transform into new forms of matter that we observe.
